File":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c0d0ce9efdbc163394137bca63118fd321cfdc716c7c4b7ea33693fd0c3ed066","compact":"3845089a92fb2dd6093b8bf65390fcb95b1abe82d4f95a2ede4f6aad0a017931","nasal":"3160b7ed89954edc8b857bd6f10744279637529e620d8cc14b9a72e51c28e650"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":15,"english":"O foremost of men, fell to reflecting, 'How can we become exempt from decrepitude and disease, and immortal.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f761ba79117a0944e2c2205a688bfa38f3f9b6606a6a3abd4f3b8f4b84bb400f","compact":"5848e65e2421d76a8e3b0da34110a9f478d64c3fa0890884e371ed9c017b5980","nasal":"5848e65e2421d76a8e3b0da34110a9f478d64c3fa0890884e371ed9c017b5980"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":16,"english":"And as they reflected, it struck them, 'By churning the ocean of milk, we must obtain ambrosia.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"508eabb0ed78515ff3d82bec0955359f19b678ddad4f4f03176ed34e532991f6","compact":"5d4ed5f9c48c129dd2f7e1e9f71f383783cb837ea6bb1975fcdc0933a3e06e78","nasal":"b64e2cb6f1db90f4e3246b4d66972c72fc12569364b1e786bdc96917a6006190"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":17,"english":"Then deciding upon churning (the ocean), those ones of immeasurable energy making Vasuki the cord, and the Mandara (hill), the stick, began to churn the deep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f5694adce1563fcded5922fb76e685e974de7ea140ebe191e9a3410bac589513","compact":"d318214186811ba124f779aa31cd3029fa9703517553ff97555bacc42259a801","nasal":"6194f7ad8e04295643718623a87795313b9ac00a01655518264fd043e4e0159b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":18,"english":"After a thousand years, had rolled on, arose a male being impregnated with the Āyurveda, of exceedingly righteous soul, called Dhanvantari, bearing in his hands a stick, and a Kamandalu. And there arose also, from the cream of the churning waters, those magnificent dames the shining Apsaras. And, O foremost of men, as they had emerged from water, they are called Apsaras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b7b41e203ac2387f699ed11d5bf2318e40b798441405a0346956dccd6c148ad","compact":"9e697ac18ac7fa228ef070cbb13a7c598041d0b92b2700de52ec55ed6ae3d258","nasal":"ad63de3043bbe4ad65e4adb50c308b78b878af091cf569d296920f239d005781"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":19,"english":"There sprang sixty koțis of shining Apsaras. And, O Kākutstha, the female attendants of those are numberless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.946,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca5ba4e50a4ab09916cc950c8360292fe0ba945d0d2835feebef26ae2303578b","compact":"00aee80ac6bb595d6cd6788a896d26cc7601ae4bd1e533a1564a56304c6a08e5","nasal":"00aee80ac6bb595d6cd6788a896d26cc7601ae4bd1e533a1564a56304c6a08e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":20,"english":"And neither the deities nor the Dānavas would accept them, and in consequence of this nonacceptance, they are known as women belonging to all.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.769,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2f369a0f99e1b199bfe4b60011911b4c914972e6e690533de7b886efdfae335","compact":"8f9cdc829264125a8d78f9c5c11c3b1585592e343db8b2555c9c1659abaf88c8","nasal":"6da54f5c2ab0af238f56239a41dec910b60763f9417a31d8687db23d36cec44a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":21,"english":"And then, O Raghu's descendant, arose the eminently pious daughter of Varuna, Varuni, who fell to looking for acceptance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb697c95101cb8077665b99ce2476c9fda8d2129e2f12f5a45444cddcd702c98","compact":"464bce2edfb173f4f507ef63b78b414d459b2fa333e68ff8efa17682b25f8cd9","nasal":"8a506d75b67ea38ab65a64ad531faf3bc88a4483e42cd92b73d40c6b74acc5ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-44-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":44,"verse":22,"english":"And Diti's sons, O Rāma, did not accept the daughter of Varuna and Aditi's sons, O hero, accepted that one of blameless limbs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-45-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1044022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11103148e158ea05a35bcada78675d77ac35ac347de5d8dd401ed655c3c41a2f","compact":"39a51765958cb30431bdd4d38af88d42903fe515311